    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Pfaadt. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable anchor, leveraging his dynamic platoon advantage to secure the highest score of the day, while **Andy Pages** receives a major boost from a favorable park factor and a slow-delivery pitcher that enhances his high-speed profile. **Jacob Wilson** (69.79) is another critical play; despite facing a lefty, his elite projection is buoyed by a significant park factor and wind blowing out, making him an essential component of our offensive engine.\n\nWhile we are rolling out a strong lineup, we must keep a close eye on the weather; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.67) is currently our only major risk factor with a 30% rain probability in his matchup against Nola. We also have to be cautious with **Liam Hicks**, whose score (45.41) is hampered by the uncertainty of a pending lineup; should he drop down in the order, we may see his efficiency dip further. Our most difficult decision was keeping **Heliot Ramos** (46.60) on the bench. While **Heliot Ramos** projected well enough to be considered, his difficult matchup against an elite arm in Sale ultimately tipped the scale in favor of our higher-floor starters. We are prioritizing total category coverage, specifically leaning into our speed-capable players like **Jackson Merrill** (66.07), who continues to thrive thanks to a positive platoon outlook and a slow opposing delivery that keeps his base-stealing potential elevated.",
